# Orbit Shorts — Related video pill only (locked 28 Aug 2026)

**Going forward:** every **new** Short’s Short → long CTA is the **Studio Related video pill** pointing at **that week’s Thursday long**. That is the only Short → long CTA.

## Do this (new Shorts)

1. In **desktop** YouTube Studio, set **Related video** → that week’s Thursday long.
2. Related target is **that week’s Thursday long only** — never another Short, never a different week’s film, never `/go/`.
3. On-screen CTA + description still name the film / parent long URL (zero `/go/` on Shorts). Related is the Studio funnel control; a pin is **not** a substitute.

## Do not (new Shorts)

- Do **not** add pinned comments on new Shorts.
- Do **not** use a pin instead of Related.
- Do **not** point Related at another Short.
- Do **not** put `/go/` on Shorts.

## Long-form pins (unchanged)

Long-form videos still get pins (detail, `/go/`, book). Do **not** remove those.

## Existing Short pins (grandfather)

Existing Short pins already live may stay. Do **not** mass-unpin. Do **not** remint to “fix” pins.

## Related targets (current window)

| Week | Thursday long | YouTube id |
|------|---------------|------------|
| Through 2 Sep | Last Star | `REXYxuLOBoI` (letter **O**, not zero) |
| From 3 Sep | Europa | `NbW5G1BpPY0` |
| Neutron week | Neutron Star | `Yk1tLh23rko` |

Update this table when the next Thursday long locks; always use **that week’s** long only.

## Auditor (ship gate)

- New Shorts **FAIL** if Related is missing, wrong target, or points at another Short.
- New Shorts **FAIL** if a **new** pin is added.
- Do **not** FAIL existing live Short pins (grandfather).
- Pin is not a substitute for Related — missing Related still FAILs even if a pin exists.

